script output: evidence items now cite individual gb test results with
per-parameter inconsistency counts (n=1: 12-13, n=2: 34-38, n=3: 66-72)
rather than the previously unimplemented row-reduction claim; Section 4
describes the pre-built coboundary approach and instructs the reader to run
`python src/C_triviality.py` to reproduce all results.

Update docs/issues/final_reflection.md line 25 to replace the stale
"213-equation row-reduction for n=1" claim with the accurate description
of individual gb tests for n=1,2,3 via the pre-built coboundary system.

